nimony learns a **Temen backend** (`nimony t`), so the self-hosted lane's driver plans the whole build.

Why: the self-hosted lane (#1609) runs nimony's own driver in-guest on Temen. With the C backend the
plan ends in lengc + cc + a linker, none of which exist there, so the host used to run hexer and the
link itself. With this backend the driver's plan is the whole build and the host only seeds sources.

What: the C backend's pipeline unchanged up to the DCE'd `.c.nif` (same target, same hexer, same
flags, so every artifact up to there is byte-identical to `nimony c`'s), then ONE whole-program
node in place of lengc + cc + link: `temen-link -o:<prog.temen> <every module's .c.nif, main
first>`, which writes one verified Temen module. It sits beside `backendWasm` (the same shape:
ithaqua is its whole-program tool), shares its output-naming helper (`wholeProgramFile`), and gets
its own backend directory (`<main>.temen/`). `nimony t -r` refuses: a Temen module runs under a
Temen host. `temen-link` itself lives in this repo (`crates/temen-run/demos/temen_link`).

Applied to a COPY of the pinned sources at build time (`scripts/ci/nim-selfhost-lane.sh`); the
vendored `nimony/` submodule is never modified. Against the submodule pin (v0.6.2, 851fe262).
Drop it when upstream nimony has a Temen backend — it is written to be upstreamed as is.
